    "about": "Doctoral Researcher in Electrical Engineering, University of Virginia (Expected Graduation: Spring 2027)\n Researcher in the Imaging and Data Science Laboratory under Prof. Gustavo K. Rohde, developing methods at the intersection of optimal transport, machine learning, mathematical modeling, and computational biology. Research focuses on generalizable frameworks for analyzing high-dimensional cellular and subcellular measurements, with applications to flow cytometry, multiplex imaging (4i/cIF), digital pathology, and spatial omics data analysis.",
